{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788491815,"nonce":"Qikf3LvKMLgIkP0LAWt+qgQj9WI=","title":"The client: prints the screen, renders the picture, never loses a result","message":"Part of the cockpit round, b4adee2. Design: RUNS/openrun-20260902/audit/COCKPIT.md\n§Where it lives (in rwa). The audit's themes T5, T6, T16. Everything here is\npython in rwa/; nothing touches the mod.\n\nSCOPE\n\n- Pretty mode prints the screen in COCKPIT.md's shape, six panels, the stop\n  line first; --json passes it through unchanged. RUNS/\u003crun\u003e/frames/\u003ctick\u003e.json\n  is written after every advance and every look.\n- `rwa render` is called after every advance, writing frames/\u003ctick\u003e.png from\n  the same dump; the screen names the path. The render exists; calling it\n  unasked is the whole change.\n- Every envelope carries the transcript run name as `run`, and a fallback from\n  an unset RWA_RUN prints a warning on stderr and stamps `run_source:\n  fallback`. This run lost 27% of its steps — the entire military build-out,\n  five of seven mech raids, nine of twenty deaths and the wipe — to a\n  conversation that started without the variable, and nothing in any envelope\n  could have shown it (T16).\n- `--wait`: a call issued while an advance is in flight waits for it to finish\n  and then runs, instead of being refused busy and lost. Eighty busy refusals\n  this run; one map-dump call site was refused 25 times of 32 (T5).\n- `rwa result \u003cid\u003e`: re-reads results/\u003cid\u003e.json for a command the client gave\n  up on. The mod always writes the result; 26 orphans this run hold cmd.json\n  and no result.json, seven of them advances that moved 106,874 ticks nobody\n  saw (T6).\n- `rwa status` writes a transcript step; today it reads status.json directly\n  and leaves no trace, including the call that discovered the game running\n  unsupervised.\n\nACCEPTANCE\n\n- selftest: a fakebench advance that replies with a screen prints all six\n  panels and writes the frame file; --json is byte-identical to the envelope.\n- An envelope from a shell with RWA_RUN unset carries run and run_source:\n  fallback and prints the warning; with it set, run_source: env.\n- A read issued during a fakebench advance with --wait returns the read's\n  result after the advance, and the transcript records both in completion\n  order.\n- rwa result on a step directory with cmd.json and no result.json recovers the\n  result and writes it into the step.\n- rwa status appears in the transcript as a step.","files":null}]}